  "answer": "A keyboard cleaning mode has been requested before. #21313 is the main open request, for a utility that disables the keyboard, mouse and touchscreen while you clean them. #33581, #29382 and #42868 were closed as duplicates of it or of related tickets. A maintainer said on #21313 that there are currently no plans to build this into PowerToys, so it isn't available. To follow it or show support, add a thumbs-up or comment on #21313 instead of opening a new ticket. In the meantime, you can disable the built-in laptop keyboard in Device Manager (Win+X, then Device Manager, then Keyboards, then Disable). You can also unplug a USB keyboard, or turn off Bluetooth for a wireless one. Other tickets mention third-party tools or AutoHotkey scripts for this."
 },
